;
; How Lodestone files one contact of net.peers' routing table in MYRA
; (lodestone_rules.h LR4): its place in the list (net.peers holds at most
; 256), its Kademlia bucket, whether it advertised UBH-168, when it was
; last seen in ms since 1970, whether the mesh book has an account for it,
; whether the owner admitted it to the commons, and the receipts still
; outstanding with it. The rules say what the values may mean; this says
; whether they make a record.
^ZXLODESTONE(contact:i3) = bucket:i3! ^ ubh:i1! ^ seen:i15! ^ book:i1! ^ member:i1! ^ pending:i9!
